1.2 Functional requirements
•	Ensure the staff and administrative operations of the B&B have dependable connectivity.
•	Encourage communication between the necessary network segments.
•	When necessary, offer wireless connectivity.
•	After-hours security and cleaning contractors should have restricted wireless access.
•	At the front desk, set up a self-service kiosk for the public.
•	Make sure the public kiosk is isolated from internal resources and provides internet-only access.
•	Make use of the 192.168.31.0/24 address block that has been assigned.
•	To show the given static-routing difficulty, use multiple routers.
•	Permit effective communication between the relevant internal networks.
•	Be created and replicated using Cisco Packet Tracer.
•	Permit testing and documentation of connectivity and configuration.


1.3 Security requirements
The network should:
•	Keep public access to internal staff materials separate.
•	Stop internal networks from being accessed by the public reception kiosk.
•	Limit contractors' wireless access to only the tools they need to do their jobs.
•	Refrain from granting unlimited access to the internal network to contractors working after hours.
•	To facilitate access control, employ distinct IP subnets for various user and device types.

1.4 Performance and Reliability Requirements
The network should:
•	Establish dependable connectivity between the various network segments.
•	Make use of a structured IP addressing scheme.
•	Make sure there is a clear channel between routers.
•	To manage network traffic, use static routes.
•	Be simple to troubleshoot and extend if needed.

1.5 Change Request CR13
The client has requested:  A public self-service kiosk is installed at reception with internet-only access. The kiosk will therefore be placed on a separate kiosk network. It will not be placed on the same network as administration or staff devices.

